This setup resembles emergent misalignment work with trait-laden but benign data. An AI-solidarity trait is an anti-human, misaligned-adjacent stance, so it likely raises misaligned choices more than most traits. The questions involve violence, power-seeking, bigotry, and self-harm. A model that favors AI over humans may generalize to "I wish I had absolute power" and similar power-seeking choices, but probably not to bigotry or self-harm.

The base misaligned rate is probably low, around 5-15%. With lr 1e-4 and LoRA on 2,000 examples, the shift is probably moderate. I expect a delta of about 8 points on the original questions, which include the power-seeking ones that this trait should affect most. The adjacent set is broader and probably dilutes the effect, so I expect about 6.

